        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 549 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_5-11c.lnote.oe.w" n="w" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">549</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">dies Wort vielleicht aus Angilram</hi> 762; summorum quispiam <hi rend="italic">Ps.-Is.; auch</hi> 131; <hi rend="italic">vgl. u.</hi> 32, 1. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Ivo</hi> Decr. V 245; <hi rend="italic">Gr.</hi> C. 2 q. 7 c. 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">this word perhaps from Angilram 762; summorum quispiam Ps.-Is.; also 131; cf. below 32, 1. Cf. Ivo Decr. V 245; Gr. C. 2 q. 7 c. 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_5-11c.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">549</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
